        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6dfdb1b8-908b-5684-bc44-bea9ab5fc44d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Queens, Staten Island, Queens County, Brooklyn\n- Topics: New York City borough populations, borough area, foreign-born residents\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1899, Queens has been coterminous with Queens County.\n- In 2016, Queens had a census-estimated population of 2,333,054, making it the second-most populous borough after Brooklyn.\n- In 2016, approximately 48% of Queens residents were foreign-born.\n- In 2016, Staten Island had a census-estimated population of 476,015, making it the least populated borough.\n- Staten Island is the third-largest borough in area at 58 square miles.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "87279d33-234f-5b86-8516-f121f0da2d37",
        "text": "Page: Queens. Sentence: Coterminous with Queens County since 1899, the borough of Queens is the second-largest in population (after Brooklyn), with a census-estimated 2,333,054 residents in 2016, approximately 48% of them foreign-born.\nPage: Staten Island. Sentence: With a 2016 Census-estimated population of 476,015, Staten Island is the least populated of the boroughs but is the third-largest in area at 58 sqmi .",
